Module: LanguageModel
Module Name: language_model
Module Description: A language model API wrapper.
Data Model JSON:
[
  {
    "role": "assistant",
    "content": "Once upon a time, in the heart of the Midwest, there was a small, humble cornfield named Cornville. This wasn't an ordinary cornfield; it was home to thousands of cornstalks, each one unique and full of life. The cornfield was nestled between rolling hills and vast blue skies, creating a picturesque scene that seemed to be straight out of a painting.\n\nIn this cornfield lived a humble cob of corn named Cornelius. Cornelius was not like the other cobs; he was taller and had a peculiar golden hue. He stood at the edge of the field, overlooking the vast expanse of green stalks and the endless sky beyond.\n\nOne day, a group of crows flew overhead, their cawing echoing through the field. Cornelius felt a strange sensation, a pull towards the horizon. He decided to follow this feeling, leaving his home behind. As he journeyed, he encountered various creatures - rabbits, squirrels, and even a wise old owl named Oliver.\n\nEach creature offered Cornelius advice on his journey, but none could explain the strange sensation he felt. Determined to find answers, Cornelius continued on his path. After days of travel, he reached a hilltop overlooking a vast ocean. It was then that he understood the pull - it was the call of the sea.\n\nCornelius realized that he was not just an ordinary cob of corn; he was destined for greatness. He decided to embark on a new journey, one that would take him far from his humble beginnings in Cornville. And so, with the wind at his back and the sun shining brightly above, Cornelius set sail towards the unknown, ready to face whatever adventures awaited him.\n\nAnd thus, the story of Cornelius, the golden cob of corn, became a legend in the Midwest, inspiring generations of cornstalks to dream big and follow their hearts."
  }
]

